From 6e5efc06c1c0bfa1ad41e712ec17e032264197bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:53:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Scope printed startup-shell pipelines with unknown
 alias names

Printed pipe input was only walked under session alias names, unlike heredocs and -c inputs. Collect printed payloads from connected pipelines into the existing nested-shell walk. Preserve plain-shell and unrelated-pipeline scopes, grouped consumers/producers and pipe-newline continuations; avoid tokenizing no-pipe generators.

Rebased onto main 5eec3bedbb, where the printed-payload iterator moved to cron/lifecycle_guard_output.py (iter_printed_shell_payloads, yielding (payload, raw_quote)). The shell_sink keyword now lives there; cron/lifecycle_guard.py is unchanged by this commit.

Proof: printf/echo x bash -l/zsh/ssh h failed before the fix (6 RED cases). After the rebase, the session-alias suite has 78 passed, and 13 of its tests fail with cron/ reverted to main. tests/cron: 4216 passed, 9 skipped. scripts/check: 20 checks OK. Before the rebase, eight targeted source mutants were killed.

Replay (pre-rebase head): 34579 distinct real terminal commands (command plus explicit workdir), 172895 old/new comparisons across none/ll/stock/zz/unknown. Changed verdict counts: none=0, ll=0, stock=0, zz=0, unknown=0. Corpus SHA256 e12b2f7b5fcde32586aaf33dc43885630e3dad1d8b59e16dcf5e5b3b76c286f0. Stored shell text was scanned, never executed. The baseline disables only the new nested-printed iterator. The replay uses the current filesystem, not historical file contents. The raw command corpus remains private.

Independent exact-head review and required CI remain shipping gates.
